<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0014" proc-id="E0505_____000003J00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Inner Compression Spring</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Free Length Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using vernier calipers, measure the free length of the spring.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="EM00801J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>47.43mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Deviation Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using a steel square and vernier calipers, measure the deviation of the spring.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A033470J03" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Limit</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Deviation 1.6mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Angle 2°</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the value is more than the maximum, replace the compression spring.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0015" proc-id="E0505_____000003K00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Intake Valve</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Overall Length Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using vernier calipers, measure the overall length of the intake valve.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A121380J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>101.71mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>101.21mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the length is less than the minimum, replace the intake valve.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Outer Diameter Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using a micrometer, measure the diameter of the valve stem.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A121378" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>5.470-5.485mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the diameter is not as specified, check the oil clearance.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Margin Thickness Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using vernier calipers, measure the valve head margin thickness.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A014597J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>1.05-1.45mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.5mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the length is less than the minimum, replace the intake valve.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0016" proc-id="E0505_____000003L00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Exhaust Valve</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Overall Length Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using vernier calipers, measure the overall length of the exhaust valve.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A121383J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>101.15mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>100.70mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the length is less than the minimum, replace the exhaust valve.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Outer Diameter Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using a micrometer, measure the diameter of the valve stem.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A121381" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>5.465-5.480mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the diameter is not as specified, check the oil clearance.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Margin Thickness Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using vernier calipers, measure the valve head margin thickness.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A121382J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>1.2-1.6mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.5mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the length is less than the minimum, replace the exhaust valve.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0017" proc-id="E0505_____000003M00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Valve Guide Bushing Oil Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a caliper gauge, measure the inside diameter of the guide bushing.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128229" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>5.510-5.530mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Calculate the oil clearance from the guide bushing inside diameter and the valve stem diameter.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Measurement Point</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Intake Side</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0.025-0.060</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Exhaust Side</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0.030-0.065</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Limit</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Measurement Point</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Intake Side</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0.08</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Exhaust Side</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0.10</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Oil clearance = guide bushing inside diameter - valve stem diameter.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the valve guide bushing.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0018" proc-id="E0505_____000003N00000">
<ptxt>Remove Intake Valve Guide Bushing</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Heat the cylinder head to 80-100°C.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using SST, tap out the intake valve guide bushing toward the combustion chamber.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036632J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09201-10000</s-number>
<s-subnumber>09201-01050</s-subnumber>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09950-70010</s-number>
<s-subnumber>09951-07100</s-subnumber>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0019" proc-id="E0505_____000003O00000">
<ptxt>Remove Exhaust Valve Guide Bushing</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Heat the cylinder head to 80-100°C.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using SST, tap out the exhaust valve guide bushing toward the combustion chamber.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036633J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09201-10000</s-number>
<s-subnumber>09201-01050</s-subnumber>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09950-70010</s-number>
<s-subnumber>09951-07100</s-subnumber>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224A000X_01_0020" proc-id="E0505_____000003P00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Valve Lifter</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Outer Diameter Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using a micrometer, measure the valve lifter diameter.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="P016860J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>30.966-30.976mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Oil Clearance Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using a caliper gauge, measure the lifter bore diameter of the cylinder head.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A129853" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>31.009-31.025mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Calculate the clearance from the valve lifter diameter and the lifter bore diameter.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.033-0.059mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.07mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
